check 1
# Client state of items-ground-many: the 1.14d client unit sets (traces/pc1/client-state/items-ground-many.cstate.jsonl, state-snapshot.md section 3 rule 5) against the ClientWorld of d2-client (state-dump --client-out); same save, seed, pokes and input as items-ground-many.
# Ground items, many classes and qualities (area G, drops): seeds fixed, then at frame 4 forty items made through the game's own creation path;
# the item seeds, classes and places are compared frame by frame (equal item seeds mean the same RNG draws).
# Spec: specs/tools/scenario-diff.md, specs/tools/poke.md.
# Result (2026-10-09, 36 items made on both sides): quality, item level,
# affix ids (magic, rare, auto), item seeds, start seed and the item stat
# lists are EQUAL on every item. Item flags (if) and file index (fi) were
# ignored until pc1-data.md Step 4 item 26 was answered (2026-10-09):
# 0x2000 is set at creation and cleared by the room clean-up at the end of
# the tick (generation.md §1.4, §3 step 5); a file index never written stays
# 0 from allocation (quality.md §1). Both are compared again; d2rs fails them
# until q-fix-p5-item-new-flag-file-index lands (done: file index 0 and the
# 0x2000 clear in the update pass). Left: the identified flag 0x10 of normal
# items (pc1-data Step 4 item 28).
name cs-items-ground-many
save ScnAma --class ama --expansion
seed 1234
ticks 30
seconds 240
channels cstate
at 4 poke seed-game 0x00001234 666
at 4 poke item hax @x+2 @y quality magic ilvl 20
at 4 poke item 2ax @x+3 @y quality rare ilvl 35
at 4 poke item bsw @x+4 @y quality unique ilvl 40
